  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 General Election (November 3, 2026)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n Courts\n Employment\n FAQ\n Public Information\n \n\n Translate Language\n \n Translate\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n About\n \n \n \n\n Cemeteries\n Communities\n County Ordinances\n Economic Development\n Elected Officials\n School Districts\n Township Information\n \n \n \n\n Departments\n \n \n \n\n 911\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor & Elections\n Board of Supervisors\n Conservation\n Economic Development\n Emergency Management\n Human Resources\n IT/GIS\n Maintenance\n Public Health\n Recorder\n Road Department\n Sheriff's Office\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n Zoning\n \n \n Visit\n Contact\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nElections \n\n2026 General Election\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \nNovember 3, 2026\n \nGeneral Election \n \n\n A General Election is an election in which all or most members of a given political body are up for election. The term is usually used to refer to elections held for a nation's primary legislative body, as distinguished from by-elections and local elections. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n \n\n \nKEY DATES: \n \n \n \n2026 General Election - Candidate Filing Period: \n \n \n \n \nNow through Wednesday, August 26, 2026 \n \nFiling Office Open until 5:00 p.m. on 8/26/26 \n \nCounty Candidates – Marion County Auditor is filing officer \n \n \n \n \nFirst day Auditor can receive Absentee Ballot Requests: \n \n \n \nTuesday August 25, 2026 \n \n \n \nFirst day to Absentee Vote at Marion County Auditor's Office 214 E Main St Knoxville, IA \n \n \nWednesday, October 14, 2026 \n \nOffice Hours: M-F - 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. \n \nPlease note ID required to participate. \n \n \n \nFirst day the Auditor's Office can mail absentee ballots to voters who have submitted requests. \n \n \nWednesday, October 14, 2026 \n \n \n \nVoter Pre-Registration Deadline    \n \n \nMonday, October 19, 2026 \n \nOffice Hours October 19, 2026 - 8:00 a.m.- 5:00 p.m. \n \n \n \nDeadline to request a mailed Absentee Ballot. \n \n \nMonday, October 19, 2026 \n \nOffice Hours October 19, 2026 - 8:00 a.m.- 5:00 p.m. \n \n \n \nAuditor’s office open Saturday \n \n \nSaturday, October 31, 2026 \n \nOffice Hours October 31, 2026 - 8:00: a.m. – 5:00 p.m. \n \n \n \nLast day to vote Absentee Ballot at the Marion County Auditor's Office, 214 E Main, Knoxville IA. \n \n \nMonday, November 2, 2026 \n \nOffice Hours November 2, 2026 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. \n \n \n \nAll Absentee Ballots, whether returning in person or by mail must be received in the Marion County Auditor’s Office by 8:00 p.m. on 11/3/2026 \n \nElection Day - Tuesday, November 3, 2026 \n \n \nPolling Hours 7:00 a.m. - 8:00 p.m. (ID required to participate) \n \nAbsentee Ballot return – In Person - deadline 11/3/26, 8:00 p.m. at the Marion County Auditor's Office, 214 E Main, Knoxville Iowa. \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n  \n \nPublic Notice\n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Results Available on Election Night\n \n \n\n 0/17 Precincts Counted\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n 2026 General Election - BU.HM.MV\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Clay - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Clay Twp\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Dallas Twp\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Franklin Twp\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Franklin Twp - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Harvey\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Indiana Twp\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Indiana Twp - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - KX1 - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - KX2 - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - KX3 - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - KX4 - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - KXT\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - KXT - KSD\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - Liberty Twp\n \n \n\n 202